1. Docstring: NO — regress/ppc_ifetch_probe.py:75-79.
   Partner-loop comment: NO — regress/ppc_ifetch_probe.py:554-557.

The proviso preserves the visits and toggled state, but does not ensure that intervening code preserves the condition.

Counterexample inserted before arm (a), DERIVED, not measured:

    if (addr == 0xfec00008ULL)
        cpu->pc ^= 0x1000ULL;

On T ra’s first failure, pc becomes 0xfec01008; the toggle leaves addr unchanged. The read-ahead loop and subfic preserve that pc (src/cpus/cpu_dyntrans.c:1957-1978; src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c:311-318). The next translator prologue preserves pc but recomputes addr as 0xfec01008 (cpu_ppc_instr.c:4099-4103). That address is unmapped: the nearby cpc700_pci window covers only 0xfec00000–0xfec00007 (src/devices/dev_cpc700.c:238-239).

The second failed-fetch visit therefore happens, with the toggled state unchanged between visits, but its condition is false. The toggle fires once and does not cancel.

2. No separate new false claim: the added rec11 counterexample and its DERIVED label are correct. What remains dangling is preservation of the predicate across visits. Both sites must additionally require the condition to have the same truth value at both failed-fetch entries and the matched partner entry. This is a records defect, not a demonstrated detector escape.

The saved rec11_proof.out reports text-only equivalence. I edited nothing and ran no build, emulator, probe or proof script.

3. VERDICT: FIX.

